This repository — including its source code, documentation, prompt
templates, starter Office templates, generated sample outputs, and every
accompanying asset (collectively, "the Work") — is a private portfolio
submission published on GitHub for the sole purpose of allowing
prospective employers and reviewers to evaluate the author's engineering
work in connection with a specific hiring process.

PERMITTED USE
-------------
- Reading, browsing, and inspecting the Work on GitHub.
- Cloning the Work to a local machine solely to run or examine it for
  the purpose of evaluating the author's candidacy.
- Quoting short, clearly attributed snippets in private correspondence
  with the author (e.g. interview feedback).

PROHIBITED USE
--------------
Without the author's prior written consent, no person or organisation
may:

  1. Copy, fork, mirror, re-publish, re-host, or redistribute the Work
     or any substantial portion of it, in any medium.
  2. Modify the Work and present the result as their own creation.
  3. Submit the Work, in whole or in part, as a response to any
     coursework, interview assignment, take-home exercise, assessment,
     certification task, hackathon entry, or similar evaluation, whether
     for academic, professional, or commercial purposes.
  4. Train, fine-tune, or evaluate machine-learning systems on the Work,
     except insofar as public code-indexing by search engines is an
     unavoidable incident of publishing on GitHub.
  5. Use the Work, or any derivative of it, in a commercial product or
     service.

